==Trivia==
*[[Version 4.0 Update|Version 4.0]] gave Kotatsu Cat the ability to [[Weaken]] Floating.
*Prior to [[Version 4.7 Update|Version 4.7]], Sadako Cat was a part of another [[Cat Combo]] called [[Electric Home (Removed Combo)|Electric Home]].
*Prior to [[Version 15.7 Update|Version 15.7]], Kotatsu Cat's descriptions read as follows:
<pre>Kotatsu Cat
Very effective in winter… not that it matters.
Damage from Floating enemies greatly reduced.
Might weaken Floating enemies.</pre>
<pre>Sadako Cat
Hid in a TV to scare people for fun.
Was never able to get out. Haunts TVs now.
Resistant to + might weaken Floating.</pre>
<pre>Octopus Cat
Extra-flexible Cat who feels most comfortable
in small, dark spaces. Wave Shield.
Tough vs Floating, might weaken enemies.</pre>
*Kotatsu Cat gets its name from the ''[[wikipedia:kotatsu|kotatsu]]'' it drags around, which is a Japanese heated table.
*Sadako Cat is a reference to [[wikipedia:Sadako Yamamura|Sadako Yamamura]], AKA Ringu, the TV-haunting ghost from the horror movie series ''[[wikipedia:The Ring (franchise)|The Ring]]''.
*Octopus Cat is based on the ''[[wikipedia:ja:蛸壺|takotsubo]]'' (蛸壺), a pot-like octopus trap used by fishermen.
*Octopus Cat's Japanese name contains all of the syllables from Kotatsu Cat's Japanese name:
**ねこタツ ''<u>Nekotatsu</u>'' (Catatsu) → ねこタコつぼ ''<u>Neko Ta</u>ko<u>tsu</u>bo'' (Cat Octopus Pot)
*Octopus Cat's Catfruit evolution description contains several inaccuracies:
**Although it claims Octopus Cat has increased attack speed, the attack speed actually decreases.
**It claims Octopus Cat gains immunity to Wave Attacks, Octopus Cat doesn't actually gain the Immune to Waves ability.
*Kotatsu Cat and its evolutions are one of the few Cat Units whose icon is not flipped.
*Kotatsu Cat, [[Lesser Demon Cat (Uber Rare Cat)|Lesser Demon Cat]] and their evolutions' sprites actually move backwards in their walking animation, as this gives the illusion of staying still. This effect is most noticeable when said units are Slowed.
*In several [[Nyanko Daisensou 4Koma & Strategy App|4Koma]] comics, it is shown that there are also three [[Cat (Normal Cat)|Cats]] under Kotatsu Cat's ''kotatsu''.

